<title>RUSSIA: Russian factory pays workers in bras.</title>
<headline>Russian factory pays workers in bras.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Russian factory facing a cash crisis is supporting its workers by paying them in bras.</p>
<p>&quot;I get paid in the factory's output, and it's convenient for me,&quot; one woman worker told Reuters on Tuesday by telephone from Volgograd's Armina factory in central Russia. &quot;You can earn up to 40 percent more than your salary by selling these items.&quot;</p>
<p>A typical employee earns 33 to 42 bras worth $2.15 each a month, the worker said. They also have the option of being paid in other types underwear -- or waiting for actual cash at a unspecified date in the future.</p>
</text>
